#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:16
msgid "Show what `dwarffs` resolves to:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:33
msgid "Show information about `dwarffs` in JSON format:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:35
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix flake metadata dwarffs --json | jq .\n"
"{\n"
"  \"description\": \"A filesystem that fetches DWARF debug info from the "
"Internet on demand\",\n"
"  \"lastModified\": 1597153508,\n"
"  \"locked\": {\n"
"    \"lastModified\": 1597153508,\n"
"    \"narHash\": \"sha256-VHg3MYVgQ12LeRSU2PSoDeKlSPD8PYYEFxxwkVVDRd0=\",\n"
"    \"owner\": \"edolstra\",\n"
"    \"repo\": \"dwarffs\",\n"
"    \"rev\": \"d181d714fd36eb06f4992a1997cd5601e26db8f5\",\n"
"    \"type\": \"github\"\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"locks\": { ... },\n"
"  \"original\": {\n"
"    \"id\": \"dwarffs\",\n"
"    \"type\": \"indirect\"\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"originalUrl\": \"flake:dwarffs\",\n"
"  \"path\": \"/nix/store/l06r23gw4psl1f547il2hbnwnxaplbaz-source\",\n"
"  \"resolved\": {\n"
"    \"owner\": \"edolstra\",\n"
"    \"repo\": \"dwarffs\",\n"
"    \"type\": \"github\"\n"
"  },\n"
"  \"resolvedUrl\": \"github:edolstra/dwarffs\",\n"
"  \"revision\": \"d181d714fd36eb06f4992a1997cd5601e26db8f5\",\n"
"  \"url\": \"github:edolstra/dwarffs/"
"d181d714fd36eb06f4992a1997cd5601e26db8f5\"\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:66
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:68
msgid ""
"This command shows information about the flake specified by the flake "
"reference _flake-url_. It resolves the flake reference using the [flake "
"registry](./nix3-registry.md), fetches it, and prints some meta data. This "
"includes:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:73
msgid ""
"`Resolved URL`: If _flake-url_ is a flake identifier, then this is the flake "
"reference that specifies its actual location, looked up in the flake "
"registry."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:77
msgid ""
"`Locked URL`: A flake reference that contains a commit or content hash and "
"thus uniquely identifies a specific flake version."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:80
msgid ""
"`Description`: A one-line description of the flake, taken from the "
"`description` field in `flake.nix`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:83
msgid "`Path`: The store path containing the source code of the flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:85
msgid "`Revision`: The Git or Mercurial commit hash of the locked flake."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:87
msgid ""
"`Revisions`: The number of ancestors of the Git or Mercurial commit of the "
"locked flake. Note that this is not available for `github` flakes."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:91
msgid ""
"`Last modified`: For Git or Mercurial flakes, this is the commit time of the "
"commit of the locked flake; for tarball flakes, it's the most recent "
"timestamp of any file inside the tarball."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:95
msgid "`Inputs`: The flake inputs with their corresponding lock file entries."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:98
msgid "With `--json`, the output is a JSON object with the following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:100
msgid ""
"`original` and `originalUrl`: The flake reference specified by the user "
"(_flake-url_) in attribute set and URL representation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:103
msgid ""
"`resolved` and `resolvedUrl`: The resolved flake reference (see above) in "
"attribute set and URL representation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:106
msgid ""
"`locked` and `lockedUrl`: The locked flake reference (see above) in "
"attribute set and URL representation."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:109
msgid "`description`: See `Description` above."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:111
msgid "`path`: See `Path` above."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:113
msgid "`revision`: See `Revision` above."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:115
msgid "`revCount`: See `Revisions` above."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:117
msgid "`lastModified`: See `Last modified` above."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-metadata.md:119
msgid "`locks`: The contents of `flake.lock`."
msgstr ""

